  "ai_language_tip": "Speak clear, polite Danish (da); English is excellent and widely accepted, especially in Copenhagen and Aarhus; Danish speech is fast with soft consonants, so ask for numbers to be repeated; German helps a little in southern Jutland.",
  "english_ok": "yes — Very high English nationwide; formal authority letters and GP lines still prefer Danish.",
  "politeness": "Informal 'du' is standard; open with 'Hej' or 'Goddag' and say whom you call for; close with 'Tak, hej hej'. Brief, relaxed tone.",
  "name_tip": "First name + surname, informal; surname alone is fine for a booking ('i navnet Jensen'); many share the same -sen surnames, so add first name; spell foreign names letter by letter.",
  "phone_tip": "All numbers are 8 digits with no trunk 0, written in pairs (12 34 56 78), +45; MobilePay is tied to the mobile number.",
  "time_tip": "TRAP: 'halv otte' = 7:30; 'kvart i otte' = 7:45; '2. th.' in addresses means 2nd floor, right door; read back in 24h.",
  "number_tip": "TRAP: tens from 50 up are vigesimal ('halvtreds' = 50, 'tres' = 60, 'halvfjerds' = 70, 'firs' = 80, 'halvfems' = 90) and units come first ('femogtyve' = 25); read phone numbers in pairs.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid lunch 11:30–12:30, dinner peak 18:00–20:00, calls after 19:00, and weekends for offices; GPs (egen læge) take phone consultations in a fixed morning telefontid.",
  "closed_days": "Shops may open on Sundays but close on public holidays (e.g. Maundy Thursday, Good Friday, Easter Monday, Ascension, Whit Monday, 24–26 December, 1 January); Store Bededag was abolished from 2024; July summer holiday closes many small firms.",
  "booking_channels": "Egen læge via the practice's telefontid, Min Læge app or sundhed.dk; restaurant web booking (DinnerBooking and own sites) and phone; online booking pages for salons; Wolt and Just Eat for delivery; MitID and MobilePay are everyday tools.",
  "voice_menu": "Egen læge telefontid, regional emergency line, Borger.dk/Skat, banks and operators (TDC/Nuuday, Telenor, Telia, 3) use IVR, often with callback.",
  "callback_habits": "Practices use call-back lists and Min Læge messages; booking systems send SMS/email reminders; small businesses reply by SMS.",
